;; demos/scenarios/clinic-decade/config.edn -- the vendoring
;; batch 2 rider (AR-VB2-R, 2026-08-07): the scenarios/ home's first
;; entry, a busy weekday mix across the twelve everyday-ambulatory and
;; acute modules vendored across the vendoring arc's first two batches
;; (sore_throat/sinusitis/bronchitis/asthma/ear_infections/urinary_tract_
;; infections/sleep_apnea/fibromyalgia/dementia/appendicitis/
;; total_joint_replacement/sepsis) plus a five-minute arrival gap for a
;; steady, busy stream. `:module-initial-attributes` seeds every
;; total-joint-replacement walk to the knee variant (ADR-0033 AR-1's own
;; attachment rule) so that closure's own content lands without relying
;; on its default attribute distribution. Landed VERBATIM from the
;; design channel's own authored copy (AR-VB2-R) -- see this directory's
;; own README.md for the runnable command and the live-probe result.
{:pathway {:name "clinic-decade" :steps []}
 :arrival-gap 5
 :modules ["sore_throat" "sinusitis" "bronchitis" "asthma" "ear_infections"
           "urinary_tract_infections" "sleep_apnea" "fibromyalgia" "dementia"
           "appendicitis" "total_joint_replacement" "sepsis"]
 :module-assignment [{:module-id "sore_throat" :weight 15}
                      {:module-id "sinusitis" :weight 12}
                      {:module-id "bronchitis" :weight 10}
                      {:module-id "asthma" :weight 10}
                      {:module-id "ear_infections" :weight 8}
                      {:module-id "urinary_tract_infections" :weight 8}
                      {:module-id "sleep_apnea" :weight 7}
                      {:module-id "fibromyalgia" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "dementia" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "appendicitis" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "total_joint_replacement" :weight 6}
                      {:module-id "sepsis" :weight 6}]
 :module-initial-attributes {"total_joint_replacement" {:total-joint-replacement/joint-replacement "knee"}}
 ;; ARC 3A PART 4 (ADR-0173 ruling D1's commit 2, 2026-08-26): the
 ;; demographic fold, TURNED ON. This is the opt-in -- `:persons` absent
 ;; is the byte-identical path, and this file is one of the six corpora
 ;; that stop taking it.
 ;;
 ;; `:count` IS TWICE THE ARRIVAL COUNT, and both the shape and the
 ;; factor are measurements rather than preferences. With `:persons`
 ;; present an arrival BINDS to a person, and a repeat arrival of
 ;; somebody already registered queues NOTHING (ADR-0173's own first
 ;; tabled deviation: a second `:admission` for a discharged patient
 ;; violates `admission-only-when-new`). So a small pool silently
 ;; deletes clinical content -- probed at `:count` 50 against 200
 ;; arrivals, only 50 patients registered and three quarters of this
 ;; scenario's own module walks never happened.
 ;;
 ;; One person per arrival is not enough either, and the generator-side
 ;; COVERAGE GATE is what said so: at `:count` 200 the birthday paradox
 ;; still makes better than a third of the arrivals repeats, and the
 ;; module coverage that thinned took this scenario's only
 ;; module-compiled `:admission`/`:discharge` pair with it --
 ;; `gated-runs-collectively-produce-every-emittable-event-type` went
 ;; red on exactly those two kinds. At twice the arrival count the
 ;; collision rate drops enough that both come back.
 ;;
 ;; `:years` IS TWENTY, not the ten `ehrt.sim.run/default-person-years`
 ;; would give, and that is a measurement too: at 10 years this
 ;; population produced ZERO occupational injuries (the hazard is
 ;; conditioned on `:employed` person-years, and most of a ten-year walk
 ;; is not), so the clinical hook would have been declared and never
 ;; witnessed. At 20 it fires. A run's own log therefore extends to the
 ;; PERSON horizon, well past its clinical content -- that is what a
 ;; demographic timeline is, and this scenario's own README carries the
 ;; re-witnessed figures.
 :persons {:count 400 :years 20}
 :module-horizon-days 3650}
